{"name":"Gran Torino Red","hex":"#ee3300","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gran","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grandmother."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grandfather. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gran"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gran Torino","blocks":[{"text":"Gran Torino is a 2008 drama film produced and directed by Clint Eastwood, who also stars in the lead role. The film features a significant Hmong American cast, a first for mainstream American films. Kyle Eastwood and Michael Stevens composed the score, while Jamie Cullum and Clint Eastwood provided the lead track."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Gran_Torino_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gran_Torino"},{"title":"Turin","blocks":[{"text":"Turin is a city and a business and cultural centre in northern Italy. It is the capital and largest city of Piedmont and of the Metropolitan City of Turin. From 1861 to 1865, it was the first capital of the Kingdom of Italy. The city is mainly on the western bank of the River Po, below its Susa Valley, and is surrounded by the western Alpine arch and Superga hill. The population of the city proper is 855,654 as of 2026, while the population of the urban area is estimated by Eurostat to be 1.7 million inhabitants. The Turin metropolitan area is estimated by the OECD to have a population of 2.2 million."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Torino_Piazza_Castello_11.jpg/330px-Torino_Piazza_Castello_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turin"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg/500px-St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg/1280px-St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg/500px-St._Ambrose_Catholic_Church_-_Grosse_Pointe%2C_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Saint Ambrose Roman Catholic Church in Grosse Pointe Park served as a shooting locatio